   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-3-1-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What does Scikit-learn's LabelEncoder library do?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Encodes data alphabetically</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. LabelEncoder encodes data alphabetically. It turns the country names into numbers in alphabetical order.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Encodes data numerically</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. It does turn country names into numbers, but the best answer names how: it encodes data alphabetically.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Encodes data serially</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. LabelEncoder encodes data alphabetically, as with the country names.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
